# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# Nenjam Matrimony — Root .gitignore
#
# This file covers repo-wide/cross-cutting concerns (secrets, editors,
# OS noise) and acts as a monorepo-safe backstop for platform build
# output. Frontend/.gitignore and backend/.gitignore own the detailed,
# tool-specific rules for their own trees — see those files first.
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# ─── OS / editor noise ────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
*.swo

# ─── Backup / patch residue ────────────────────────────────────────
# Dropped next to the real file by editors, `git merge`, and manual
# "copy it before I change this" edits — e.g. a gradle-wrapper.properties
# .bak left behind while working around a local Gradle download failure.
# Always machine-specific, and dangerous to commit precisely because the
# name looks so close to the real file.
*.bak
*.orig
*.rej

# ─── IDEs / AI tooling ───────────────────────────────────────────────
# Only the personal/machine-specific VS Code files are ignored —
# extensions.json / tasks.json / launch.json (team-shared recommendations
# and the "Start Development" USB-debug launch config) stay trackable.
.vscode/settings.json
.idea/
*.iml

# Claude Code — settings.local.json holds per-machine permission
# allowlists (e.g. which Bash commands are auto-approved) and is
# personal, same treatment as .vscode/settings.json above. Any shared
# CLAUDE.md / commands / agents living under .claude/ stay trackable.
**/.claude/settings.local.json

# ─── Environment files ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# Real secrets must never be committed, from either root or a nested
# app. `.env.example` (committed, no real values) is the only
# exception.
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local
.env.*
!.env.example

# ─── Firebase / cloud service credentials ──────────────────────────
serviceAccountKey.json
*serviceAccount*.json
firebase-adminsdk*.json
firebase/*.json
backend/firebase/*.json
google-services.json

# ─── Private keys, certs, keystores ────────────────────────────────
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
*.crt
*.jks
*.keystore
key.properties
**/android/key.properties

# ─── Node / NestJS (repo-wide backstop) ────────────────────────────
node_modules/
dist/
build/
coverage/
logs/
*.log
npm-debug.log*
pnpm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.nest/
tmp/
.cache/
.claudecode/
.claude/    

# ─── Flutter (repo-wide backstop; Frontend/.gitignore is primary) ──
.dart_tool/
.packages
.flutter-plugins
.flutter-plugins-dependencies
.pub/
.pub-cache/

# ─── Android (repo-wide backstop for any android/ dir in the tree) ─
**/android/local.properties
**/android/.gradle/
**/android/**/build/
**/android/**/captures/
**/android/**/outputs/
**/android/**/intermediates/
**/android/**/*.apk
**/android/**/*.aab
**/*.jks
**/*.keystore
**/**/mapping.txt
**/**/*.mapping

# ─── iOS / macOS / Linux / Windows Flutter ephemeral dirs ──────────
**/ios/Pods/
**/ios/.symlinks/
**/ios/Flutter/Flutter.framework
**/ios/Flutter/Flutter.podspec
**/ios/Flutter/ephemeral/
**/macos/Flutter/ephemeral/
**/linux/flutter/ephemeral/
**/windows/flutter/ephemeral/

# ─── Local uploads / scratch (repo root only — not assets/l10n) ───
/temp/
/tmp/
/uploads/
/cache/

# ─── UI prototypes / design assets (not part of the shipped app) ──
nenjam ui/

# ─── Seed photo ORIGINALS (local only) ───────────────────────────
#
# The seeder reads photos/profile_NN.jpg — those ARE committed, because the
# fake-profile seeder needs them to exist on any machine that runs it.
#
# The unprocessed originals they were cropped from are deliberately not.
# They are full-resolution photographs of real people; committing them would
# put those images into git history permanently, distributed to every clone
# and fork, and removing them later would need a history rewrite. The
# processed 1080x1080 crops are all the seeder needs.
photos/WhatsApp*
